{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed and verified. Summary:\n\n**Why the second publish returned 500**\n\n`similarity()` in `src/app.py` returned a Python `float` (`round()` of blended divisions), and those scores go into the `similar` list of the item passed to `put_item`. boto3 rejects floats client-side with the exact `TypeError` in `logs/error.log`. The first publish succeeded only because the table was empty — `related()` returned `[]`, so no float existed (`similar=0` in the log). From the second publish on, there is an existing story, a score gets computed, and every write dies during serialization.\n\n**The fix**\n\n- `src/app.py:31` — convert at the boundary: `Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))`. `Decimal(str(...))` keeps the exact 4-decimal rounding instead of inheriting binary-float noise.\n- `tests/test_publish.py` — new regression test `test_publish_with_existing_story_stores_similar_scores` seeds the table with one record, publishes a second story, and asserts the stored scores are `Decimal` — the input the fake table (like real boto3) rejects as floats.\n\n**Verification**: `python3 -m unittest discover tests` passes (2 tests), and the exact production scenario through `handler()` now returns 201 on both publishes, with the second storing `similar: [{'slug': 'why-my-cron-ran-twice', 'score': Decimal('0.2965')}]`.\n\n**ANSWER.md** documents the cause, the fix, and which parts of the colleague's note applied (float→Decimal root cause, empty-first-write explanation, seeded-table test), which were adapted (kept fractional scores rather than integer percentages), and which were ignored (no real-table deploy — the fake table reproduces the serializer's rejection)."}
